    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-01T15:55:46+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-01T15:55:46+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T06:25:46Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T06:25:46Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A cold front will move across SA on Tuesday. A high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and another cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough will move over SA during the day followed by a cold front early Saturday. Another high pressure ridge will move across during Sunday ahead of a low pressure system expected to develop in the far west later in the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW012" description="Lower Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-01T15:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T05:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, becoming less likely later this evening. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h turning southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Light winds becoming westerly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 3:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly and light becoming northerly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then turning west to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 25 to 35 km/h tending southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 12 with daytime temperatures reaching around 17.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
